  {
   "kind": "broken",
   "sev": "high",
   "text": "Tapping Done on a quick reading's report (finishQuickReading) runs updateCompositeRecoveryScore on the quick session, which fetches and stores sleepSnapshot/vitalsSnapshot and stamps a composite recoveryScore onto it (SessionAcceptanceService.swift:398-425, 473-475). The streaming code says a quick reading carries no recovery score (RRCollector+Streaming.swift:206-209) and the device path refuses snapshots on non-overnight captures because the newest snapshot-bearing session hijacks the Dashboard sleep chip (RRCollector+DeviceRecording.swift:494-506). DashboardSessionPolicy.latestWithSleep/latestWithVitals pick the first session with a snapshot, so a daytime quick check becomes the Dashboard's sleep/vitals source and gets a recovery score; with export enabled its metrics also go to Apple Health.",
   "evidence": [
    "Emuqu/Sources/Views/RecordView+Sections.swift:438",
    "Emuqu/Sources/Services/SessionAcceptanceService.swift:416",
